Good afternoon Melanie,

I hope you are well.

Further to James' email, please feel free to come to me for any questions you may have in his absence.

I have spoken with Aviva and they confirm the funds have been sent from True Potential today (they say allow 5 working days for the payment to complete, then you'll be able to view them on the Aviva Platform once your money has been invested).

With regards to your Quilter transfer, Quilter do need another signature from you on the form. Unfortunately, when we set up your Docusign, we didn't realise it only signed one part of the form. Apologies for this oversight.

I have attached the form for if you have access to a printer and are able to sign Section 1 on the form and email it back to me.

I will also pop the form in the post today for you 1st class with a pre-paid (just in case you do not have access to a printer). Once received back we will email this straight across to Aviva as a matter of urgency.

Any questions around this, let me know, otherwise I look forward to receiving the form from you.

Kind regards

Marie Crowther

